            <ArticleTitle>Evaluation of beta-endorphin/beta-lipotropin immunoreactivity content in the CSF of patients affected by deafferentation pain syndromes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>181-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Beta-endorphin/beta-lipotropin immunoreactivity (BE/BLPH-IR) content was evaluated in the CSF of patients suffering by deafferentation pain syndromes. BE/BLPH-IR CSF concentrations of these patients were compared with those obtained in a group of patients affected by low back pain and in a control group without pain problems. No statistically significant variation in BE/BLPH-IR levels were found between controls and subjects with different types of chronic pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
